                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_224">Glastonbury, Somerset.
                        Benedictine Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Oriel Coll. 15, or
                        its exemplar, was written in 1389 by a Glastonbury monk: inscription at end
                        of art. 2 (Holcot) erased, but legible by u.v. light: "Scriptus fuerat iste
                        liber de industria fratris Nicholai ffawkes monachi Glastonie anno domini
                        trecentesimo octogesimo nono quo tempore plures questiones de opere holkoth
                        graue fuerat inuenire" (fol. 210r) in the hand of arts. 2--6. This may have
                        been copied from the exemplar.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Bought for Oriel by Th. Wyche in 1454 from
                     the stationer John More: see The Dean's Register of Oriel College, Oxford Hist.
                     Soc., p. 389.</provenance>
